The condition is:
```c
if (result == GNUTLS_E_ASN1_ELEMENT_NOT_FOUND ||
    result != GNUTLS_E_ASN1_VALUE_NOT_FOUND) {
    return 0;
}
```

This means:
- If result is ELEMENT_NOT_FOUND → return 0 (OK)
- If result is NOT VALUE_NOT_FOUND → return 0 (OK)

So the only error that propagates is when result IS VALUE_NOT_FOUND. But the comment says "it is ok to not have parameters in SPKI". So both ELEMENT_NOT_FOUND and VALUE_NOT_FOUND should be OK. The bug is that VALUE_NOT_FOUND is NOT treated as OK.

